preConditionHook:
// ONE ATR-SIZED RISK DRIVES BOTH LEGS. Brooks's initial risk is fixed at ENTRY:
// stopAtrMultiple * ATR(atrLength) is that risk, captured ONCE on the fill bar
// and frozen for the life of the trade, and the target is rewardRisk times it.
// Re-reading the ATR every bar would let a later volatility burst widen a stop
// that was already accepted, which is a different rule.
//
// Not AtrProfitTarget (re-reads the ATR every bar, and is a target only) and not
// AtrTrailingStop (trails from the position's PEAK profit). One parameter drives
// both legs, which is why this is one rule and not two.
//
// THE CAPTURE is StopAtSignalBarRangeMultiple's: BarsSinceEntry() is 0 on the
// bar the entry FILLS and 0 while flat (EL_FEATURES.md `barssinceentry`,
// VERIFIED, and it restarts through a reversal), so the capture re-arms on every
// flat bar and is correct on the fill bar. It is NOT a MarketPosition() == 0
// reset, which skill section 4 forbids because a reversal never passes flat.
//
// WFSafe_AvgTrueRange: MultiWalk's ROLLING accumulator, ported from
// AtrProfitTarget. Seeded with a full N-term sum on the study's first calculated
// bar (MaxBarsBack + 1) and re-seeded when the length changes -- which is what
// makes the wrapper walkforward safe -- and updated thereafter as TWO
// statements, because EasyLanguage evaluates S[1] + in - out left to right and
// folding it to S += in - out is a different rounding. It is computed
// unconditionally on every bar, as the twin's unconditional function call is, so
// the accumulator advances whatever the position is; only the capture is gated.
//
// atrLen is the local length counter, atrLength the input.
if (atrLen != (int)atrLength) {
    atrSum = 0.0;
    for (int i = 0; i < (int)atrLength; ++i) {
        double hiI = high[i] > close[i + 1] ? high[i] : close[i + 1];
        double loI = low[i] < close[i + 1] ? low[i] : close[i + 1];
        atrSum += hiI - loI;
    }
    atrLen = (int)atrLength;
} else {
    const int outBar = (int)atrLength;
    double hiIn = high[0] > close[1] ? high[0] : close[1];
    double loIn = low[0] < close[1] ? low[0] : close[1];
    double hiOut = high[outBar] > close[outBar + 1] ? high[outBar] : close[outBar + 1];
    double loOut = low[outBar] < close[outBar + 1] ? low[outBar] : close[outBar + 1];
    atrSum += hiIn - loIn;
    atrSum -= hiOut - loOut;
}
atrValue = atrSum / (int)atrLength;
if (el_eq((double)ctx.BarsSinceEntry(), 0.0)) {
    riskPts = stopAtrMultiple * atrValue;
}
